{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the documentation rewrite at head 4436d508afad29f0d1fcf90221668d8501b817ca, tree 7a9e40c4, for request c31315a1 and review request a1a727f8. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED.\n\nI read the review record first, then the diff, against the request's conditions. Two independent reads ran beside mine: one compared normative rules in base and head, and one tested the rewritten claims against the source. I confirmed the items below in both versions or in the code.\n\nThe rewrite does what it set out to do. The index follows a reading journey, the evidence left the reader pages, most limits survive as close paraphrase, and a tested walk through `cli.md` and the tutorials' commands holds. Two conditions fail: I found stale facts that the record's table does not list, and the rewrite loses or changes some rules that people rely on. The relocated-text note is history, so a rule that moved only there is lost to a reader.\n\n## Changes requested: wrong claims\n\n1. A reader who follows `run-your-app.md` stops at Step 3.\n   - Step 1 sends the reader to `self-host.md`, then Step 3 runs `dap install --plan ... --cohort application`.\n   - With `DEPLOYMENT` set, the default creation policy admits only the publication and unpublished families (`packages/scope/src/creation-versions.ts:10-11`). `apps/room/wrangler.jsonc` has no `PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS`, so `platform:register@5` is refused with `unsupported-definition`. `wrangler.lending.jsonc:20` sets the six application pins, which is how the recorded run worked.\n   - No step names the setting. Fix: add it to the steps.\n\n2. The answers are still wrong in places.\n   - `manual/life-of-an-act.md:74-76`: \"No act gets that answer.\" A repeated act whose entry lies below the floor gets `{answer:\"archived\"}` (`packages/scope/src/core.ts:676-678`, `packages/contract/src/result.ts:74-79`). `scopes.md` has this right.\n   - \"Four answers\" remains at `what-is-dap.md:46` and `:160`, `architecture.md:69` and `README.md:45`, although the record says the copies were reconciled to five.\n\n3. `write-an-application.md:318-319` imports `validatePackage` from `@generalbusiness/dap-derive`. Derive does not export it. It lives in `packages/platform/src/validate-package.ts`, and the CLI imports it from `@generalbusiness/dap-platform/package-validation`. A copied import fails.\n\n4. Two pages contradict the others on what a new person can do.\n   - `what-is-dap.md:136`: \"There is no hosted sign-up. You enter a room in one of two ways.\" `wrangler.demo.jsonc` configures Browser Start, and `deploy.md`, `roadmap.md` and `README.md` describe it.\n   - `roadmap.md:30`: \"A room installs a trusted package in one act.\" `cli.md` and `self-host.md` say that no current family installs ordinary packages in a new room.\n\n5. `public-sdk-release.md:114-122` labels a column \"Published exports\", but it matches the plan in `scripts/public-release.json`, not what npm serves at `0.1.0-dev.2`. In that release platform and client export only `.`, and derive has no `./field-types`. Label it as the plan. The independent read checked this with `npm view`; I did not repeat it.\n\n6. The record's own table has one wrong row and one imprecise row. \"Eighteen, two of which the hosted endpoint omits by default\": `packages/mcp/src/hosted-tools.ts:4` omits eight, and `mcp.md` lists the eight correctly. The public-SDK row says `./package-validation` is missing, which is true only of npm.\n\n## Changes requested: rules lost or changed\n\n7. The kernel filing gate (`docs/kernel.md`).\n   - Base: \"A head that adds to the kernel names the K item that it closes, or the planner holds it.\" Head: absent. Section 7.1's waiting rule survives, but nothing says who holds a head.\n   - Base: \"fixes for the filed security findings, R1 to R16 and D1 to D6\". Head: \"fixes for filed security findings\". A closed list became an open class, so any future finding is exempt from waiting.\n   - Restore both. Role-neutral wording is fine, if the duty stays.\n\n8. Which heads the evidence rule covers (`docs/testing.md`). Base: \"applies to heads filed after ruling `fcab078d`\". Head: notes and manifests in the tree before 25 October 2026 stay as they are. The test moved from filing date to tree date, and a head filed earlier and landed later now reads differently. Say the same thing as before.\n\n9. Who deploys, and from what (`docs/deploy.md`).\n   - Base: \"From the reviewed checkout\" and \"after exact-head review\", with `ARTROOM_REPO=/absolute/path/to/the-reviewed-checkout`. Head: `DAP_REPO=/absolute/path/to/the-checkout`. No page under `docs/` now says that a deployment comes from reviewed source.\n   - Base: \"reviewed `--var` values still override them and need review\". Head: \"Repeat any `--var` overrides that the Worker needs.\"\n   - State both rules for an operator in plain terms.\n\n10. The rollout rules for creation versions. These are now only in the relocated note, and `docs/security/settings.md` still links to `deploy.md` for them:\n    - \"R1 admits one configured register root ... Use a separate Worker or an explicitly planned root cutover\";\n    - \"Do not replan an attempted or acknowledged install to make it fit the new defaults\";\n    - \"Do not treat the manifest or the fixed index as a global live-scope inventory\";\n    - \"A complete registered-scope census proves neither an empty legacy fleet nor permission to retire a definition version\".\n    - Bring them back to `deploy.md`. `dap-commons` is about to rest on them.\n\n11. Duties that became options.\n    - `mcp.md`, base: \"The planner must explicitly renew live hosted-agent tokens as a deployment step and record that step.\" Head: \"To keep such an agent, renew its bearer.\" Base also forbade claiming complete cleanup while dormant registries remain lazy. Head: \"To clean every registry, activate each one.\" Keep the prohibition and the duty.\n    - `scopes.md` loses \"Waiting does not guarantee a later admission; standing is checked again\" and \"suppression grants no license\". Restore them, since a client author relies on them.\n    - `public-sdk-release.md` loses \"Browser cross-origin access is not established by packaging\". Restore it.\n\n12. Citations that the rewrite broke.\n    - `apps/room/docs/lanes.md:451` cites `scopes.md`, \"Definitions are data\" and \"Composition\". The headings are now \"Definitions\" and \"Composition and delivery\".\n    - `packages/cli/test/demo-config.test.ts:70` cites \"until 8 November 2026 (docs/deploy.md)\". The page no longer says this. `wrangler.jsonc` does, so point at that, or restore the date on the page.\n    - `packages/bytes/src/records.ts:217` cites `docs/kernel.md` section 7 for Revision 21, which is now only in the relocated note. Keep the sentence in section 7, or change the citation. A change to `records.ts` is a source change, so prefer keeping the sentence.\n\n## Changes requested: form\n\n13. `docs/README.md` has no `## Source` footer, which the request's condition asks of every page. If the planner means to exempt the index and the two generated pages, the record should say so.\n14. `use-cases.md:327` names \"Codex CLI sessions\" in public material. Say \"Agents take part through dap's MCP server\". `claim` remains at `write-an-application.md:113` and `:248` and `ten-terms.md:104`, where the command is `create`. \"Cohort\" and \"family\" are both used for one thing, which `ten-terms.md` defines as cohort. Slice names remain at `roadmap.md:153-154` (F1, F2, F3).\n\n## What holds\n\n- `docs/lanes-reference.md` is unchanged, and `settings`, `entry-points`, MCP and kernel-boundary checks all pass, so the test-enforced regions hold.\n- The six-family table, the `--host` rule, the health fields, the self-host bindings and migrations, the pages refusals and the twelve-package and nine-input counts match the source.\n- The rules of \"Follow-up after a gate\" are all present, including the single-file exception and its conditions. The section 7 list of additions, promises and the `kernel-approved-libraries` markers are unchanged. \"The reviewer assesses\" for \"The checker must assess\" keeps the rule.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 5dc9765f gives the head tree 7a9e40c4, and from the checkpoint d10d1530 to the head only the record and the manifest change.\n- Every source path outside `docs/`, `notes/` and the root README matches main, apart from five anchors in `apps/room/docs/ledger.md`.\n- The evidence verifies. All 17 listed files match, the directory has 47 files, `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean, and no file is unlisted or writable. The gate log passes all five stages.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 951 links, 0 broken. check-commit-messages: 2 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check`: clean. My reruns of the settings and entry-point tests pass 13 of 13.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. check-notes warns on the 120,318-byte relocated-text note, against the 40,960-byte limit. The note is a record, not an implementation note, and it stays one file by decision. The record should say that the warning is expected.\n2. In-flight heads edit these pages: DX-A2, BO1 and the S1 branch all change `docs/kernel.md`, `docs/scopes.md`, `docs/mcp.md` or `docs/deploy.md`. Whichever lands second must merge by hand. BO1's rulings also ask for more text on the pages this head reshapes, so the planner should choose the order.\n3. Section 7 no longer holds its record of earlier kernel additions, which the relocated note now carries. That is a fair choice for a reader's page, but the section should link to the note, so that a reviewer can find each past reason.\n4. Three \"not run\" wordings remain in the footers. `self-host.md:8-9` and `demo.md:11-12` open with run history that belongs in the footer. `what-is-dap.md` ends with an imperative section inside an explanation, and `deploy.md` holds reference tables inside a how-to.\n5. Unresolved: `self-host.md:13` and `celld.md:5` say Node 26, while `package.json` engines says `\u003e=22`. `self-host.md:131` says \"enrolls you as the owner\", though no role has that name. `hosts.md`'s \"Each read ... revokes it\" sits beside `pages.md`'s reused site tokens, and they may describe two paths. The body of `use-cases.md`, most of `roadmap.md` and `application-views.md`'s numeric bounds were checked only lightly.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe reading journey is clear, and moving no file was the right choice: the room pages have inbound links and scripts that name their paths. Approved, apart from items 9 and 10, where a reader loses the deploy rules.\n\n## Security\n\nThe security pages keep their limits, and the test-enforced tables are unchanged. Items 7 and 9 to 11 remove duties that protect a release: who may hold a kernel head, deploying from reviewed source, reviewing `--var`, and not claiming clean-up that hasn't happened. Changes requested, items 7 and 9 to 11.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe pages shrink by about 7,700 words, one name replaces several, and duplicated explanations collapse. The work is good. Approved, with items 2 and 14 finishing it.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved, apart from items 9 and 10.\n- Security: changes requested, items 7 and 9 to 11.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: the gate, doc links, the six MCP test files, the security tests and the unchanged regions all hold. Two conditions fail: stale facts remain that the record's table doesn't list (items 1 to 5), and `docs/README.md` has no footer. Items 7 to 12 restore rules and citations.\n\nA head that makes these changes can come back for a review of its diff from this head. If it changes only documents, the documents-only rule applies, and the tests that read `docs/mcp.md`, `docs/security/*` and the lane reference run again.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a017b754f90816ed04edfa153251e219a988f66f","binding":"assigned","head":"4436d508afad29f0d1fcf90221668d8501b817ca","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a9459e2ec13b6a3a860fa13e6a80f6823adc5bed\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:547c0c7f376a47d7ed48158feab9ebc7c6f79fec\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:459293fa263d725f07590d91a8097ba8341f3909","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}